        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01J9PySuYWJqcd5P2wVMf2aJ",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: Architectural pattern of centralizing critical decisions at a single startup location to prevent scattering across the codebase.\\ntimestamp: 2025-04-03T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - pattern/Composition\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages explicitly describe the same pattern applied to different domains (credentials and paths). The connection is structural, not inferential.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2025-10-03\\n---\\n\\nBoth [[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] employ the same architectural pattern: they centralize a critical decision at a single, well-defined startup location rather than scattering that decision across the codebase.\\n\\n**Credential Scoping**: The Anthropic API key is injected into the child process environment in exactly one place \u2014 at the moment the Ingest or Query agent spawns \u2014 rather than allowing multiple parts of the codebase to read or set credentials independently.\\n\\n**Runtime Paths**: Every file-system location is resolved in a single path resolver at startup, consuming a unified configuration (command line, environment, config file, or defaults). No other part of the codebase discovers locations on its own.\\n\\nIn both cases, the benefit is the same: **correctness, auditability, and security follow from knowing there is exactly one place where the decision is made**. You cannot accidentally leak a credential from code that never reads it; you cannot accidentally use the wrong path when all paths flow through a single validator. Adding a new credential or location means extending one composition point, not searching through and modifying dozens of places.\\n\\nThis pattern is particularly valuable in systems where **the downstream decisions flow deterministically from the startup decision** \u2014 credentials and paths are both decisions that, once made, should not change during the process\u0027s lifetime. The single composition point ensures both are locked in and fully visible at one place where human review and testing can focus.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
